<title>UK: UK business starting to worry over sterling - Clarke.</title>
<headline>UK business starting to worry over sterling - Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British business is starting to worry about sterling's exchange rate, Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Speaking to Parliament, he gave no indication of his own view of whether the pound's recent rise was desirable or not.</p>
</text>
